Tue Oct 27 06:32:08 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.2.18:
  * Default delta-channel snapshots to every 100 updates
    instead of 1000 to bound replay latency
  * Let node error_handler recover on the executor path and
    stream failed task results
  * Stream the last checkpoint of a run stopped by
    interrupt_after or the recursion limit
  * Stop duplicating tags at every subgraph level

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Oct 25 06:00:00 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.2.17:
  * Apply an explicit recursion_limit equal to the default
  * Keep the caller's namespace in RemoteGraph.stream
    with subgraphs
  * Drop precautionary third-party upper bounds

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Oct 17 06:28:17 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.2.16:
  * BinOpChannel restores threads written while the field
    was a DeltaChannel
  * Pregel tracks tasks written during the run for exit mode
  * An invalid resume value no longer cuts off a task
    answered in the same resume

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Oct 15 04:52:30 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.2.15:
  * Give every message written to a messages DeltaChannel an id
  * Save cached node writes like a node that ran
  * Stop at interrupt_before when a drain is requested before it
  * Keep exit runs and update_state writes on their own checkpoints
  * Scope DeltaChannel input read-back and snapshots to own checkpoints
  * Stop ToolNode swallowing invalid resume values
  * Stop astream_events dropping control/interrupts on v1/v2
  * Raise minimum langgraph-checkpoint to >= 4.3.0

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Oct  8 06:30:10 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.2.14:
  * Raise minimum langgraph-sdk to >=0.4.6, which
    percent-encodes thread_id and assistant_id in thread
    stream requests
  * No langgraph code changes, dependency floor only

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Oct  6 07:16:10 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.2.13:
  * Fix DeltaChannel forks: replay the update checkpoint the
    thread moved past, and never replay an abandoned branch
    into a fork
  * Keep update_state on an older checkpoint out of its other
    branches, and keep the channel counters on every such path
  * Hydrate subgraph delta channels with the caller-resolved
    saver, and stop reporting answered interrupts in get_state
  * No dependency changes

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Sep 22 17:12:14 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.2.12:
  * interrupt() takes a response_schema describing the value
    expected on resume; a pydantic model, TypedDict or dataclass
    also validates the resumed value and is what interrupt()
    returns, while a plain JSON Schema dict is only surfaced
  * Interrupt carries that schema, so a client can render a typed
    input form for the resume value
  * Subgraphs are detected by walking a node function's bytecode
    instead of parsing its source, so nodes whose source cannot
    be read are no longer skipped
  * The on-demand v3 stream projections updates, custom,
    checkpoints, debug and tasks are declared on the run stream
    objects, and reading one whose transformer was not registered
    raises an AttributeError naming the registered projections

-------------------------------------------------------------------
